 "text": "Donatello went looking for a world where computers already existed, and found one experiment in America: 'Ask Mabel', the medical receptionist you could book online. In Europe: nothing. And remember 2006: no iPhone, no apps, no cloud. Two doctors out of three kept their appointments on paper. They called the third friend in Valencia, because there was no AI to ask. He and Gef built the first product together, starting from an open-source project and rebuilding it piece by piece, with help from Spanish collaborators. So, somewhere between 2005 and 2006, three friends founded a company. Tuotempo was born remote: Bologna on one end, Valencia on the other, Skype in between, and a cheap flight every now and then.",
